---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/urls';

const CONTACT = 'business@tacticalsolutions.com';

const navLinks = [
  { label: 'How it works', href: '#how-it-works' },
  { label: 'Proof', href: '#proof' },
  { label: 'For MSSPs', href: '#for-mssps' },
  { label: 'Design partners', href: '#design-partners' },
];

const metrics = [
  {
    label: 'Median alert-to-action',
    desc: 'Across all severities, all design partners.',
  },
  {
    label: '% of alerts closed without human touch',
    desc: 'The rest escalate with full context.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Design-partner retention',
    desc: 'After the first 90 days.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ProSentinel"
  description="The SOC that handles the other 22 hours. ProSentinel triages every alert, runs the playbook, and acts on the ones that matter. A human is in the loop only for the calls that need one."
  canonicalPath="/prosentinel"
  brandLabel="ProSentinel"
  brandHref="/prosentinel"
  navLinks={navLinks}
  navCta={{ label: 'Become a design partner', href: '#design-partners' }}
  wide
>
  <section id="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Autonomous SOC</p>
    <h1>The SOC that handles the other 22 hours.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Your team can run point for two hours a day. ProSentinel runs the other
      twenty-two — triaging alerts, deciding what matters, and acting on the ones
      that do. A human is in the loop only for the calls that actually need one.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="#design-partners">Become a design partner</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="#how-it-works">See the loop</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-proof">
      Built by Tactical Solutions. Currently onboarding design partners across
      mid-market SecOps and MSSPs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="problem">
    <h2>Your SOC sleeps. The threat doesn't.</h2>
    <p>
      A 24×7 SOC is two hours of real attention spread across twenty-four. The
      rest is queue. Analysts triage what they can, escalate what they have to,
      and miss what they don't see. By the time someone looks at the Tuesday 2
      a.m. anomaly, it's Wednesday morning and it's already a ticket.
    </p>
    <p>
      Hiring more analysts does not fix this. The work that breaks coverage is
      the work nobody wants — repetitive alert triage, lookups across five tools,
      the same playbook for the eightieth time this week. The good people quit.
      The queue grows.
    </p>
    <p>
      ProSentinel takes that queue. It triages every alert, runs the lookups,
      executes the playbook, and closes what closes. What's left for your team is
      the small set of decisions that actually need a human.
    </p>
    <p class="aside-link">
      Read the argument in full: <a href={withBase('/pov/the-other-22-hours')}>The other 22 hours</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works">
    <h2>See. Decide. Act.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      ProSentinel runs a closed loop on every alert that hits your stack. No
      tickets queued for someone to maybe look at later.
    </p>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>See.</h3>
        <p>
          ProSentinel ingests every signal your SIEM, EDR, identity, and network
          tools already produce. It correlates across them in real time and
          reconstructs what actually happened — not what each tool reported in
          isolation.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Decide.</h3>
        <p>
          For each correlated event, ProSentinel runs your playbook. It checks
          identity, asset criticality, recent context, and known-bad patterns. It
          produces a decision with the evidence attached. If the decision is
          below the threshold you set, it acts. If it's above, it escalates with a
          one-screen brief.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Act.</h3>
        <p>
          ProSentinel executes the response — isolate the host, disable the token,
          push the policy, open the ticket — through your existing tools. Every
          action is logged, reversible where it should be, and visible in your SOC
          console.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="sub-line">
      No new console for your team to live in. ProSentinel runs inside the stack
      you already have.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="capabilities">
    <h2>What ProSentinel handles autonomously.</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Alert triage.</h3>
        <p>Every alert from your SIEM/EDR/identity stack, correlated and ranked. Nothing sits in a queue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Identity events.</h3>
        <p>Impossible-travel, MFA fatigue, token theft, anomalous OAuth grants — investigated end to end.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Endpoint response.</h3>
        <p>Isolate, contain, kill process, snapshot — through your existing EDR, with full audit trail.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Phishing + email.</h3>
        <p>Header analysis, URL detonation, user notification, mailbox-wide pull. Handled.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Insider + data movement.</h3>
        <p>Flagged exfil patterns matched to user, role, and recent context — escalated only when warranted.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Compliance evidence.</h3>
        <p>Every action logged in a form your auditors recognize. SOC 2, ISO 27001, regulator-ready exports.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="footnote">Coverage and integrations expand each release.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="trust">
    <h2>Humans where they actually matter.</h2>
    <p>
      We do not ship "fully autonomous" as a marketing claim. ProSentinel runs
      autonomously inside the boundary you draw. You set the thresholds. You set
      the actions ProSentinel can take without asking. You see every decision it
      makes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The result: your analysts stop closing P5 tickets and start working
      incidents. Your director stops staffing for queue depth and starts staffing
      for judgment.
    </p>
    <ul class="rule-list">
      <li>Action thresholds are configurable per playbook, per asset class, per time of day.</li>
      <li>Every autonomous action is one click to reverse, with the evidence attached.</li>
      <li>Every escalation arrives as a one-screen brief — what happened, what ProSentinel did, what's left to decide.</li>
      <li>Every decision is auditable end to end, indefinitely.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="proof">
    <h2>Measured, not claimed.</h2>
    <p class="lede">These are the numbers we will publish. None of them are claimed yet.</p>
    <div class="metric-grid">
      {
        metrics.map((metric) => (
          <div class="metric">
            <p class="metric-label">{metric.label}</p>
            <p class="metric-value">Tracked since day one</p>
            <p class="metric-desc">{metric.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="who-for">
    <h2>Built for two operators.</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card" id="for-mssps-anchor">
        <h3>Mid-market SecOps.</h3>
        <p>
          500–5,000-person organizations already paying for a SOC, MDR, or
          internal security team. You have coverage on paper and gaps in practice.
          ProSentinel closes the gaps without doubling headcount.
        </p>
        <p class="card-cta"><a href="#design-partners">Talk to us</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" id="for-mssps">
        <h3>MSSPs.</h3>
        <p>
          Service providers running a shared SOC across dozens of customers. You
          need 10× operator leverage without 10× analyst hires. ProSentinel runs as
          a tier-one analyst across every tenant.
        </p>
        <p class="card-cta"><a href="#design-partners">Talk to us</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="design-partners">
    <h2>Design-partner pricing.</h2>
    <p>
      ProSentinel is in design-partner phase. Pricing is per-environment, anchored
      to the cost of the analyst hours we replace, with a fixed fee while we're
      still tuning together. Net-new general availability pricing publishes once we
      lock the second cohort.
    </p>
    <form id="intake" class="intake" novalidate>
      <p class="intake-intro">
        Apply to be a design partner. Five fields, one email.
        <a id="intake-cta" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>Apply to be a design partner</a>
      </p>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-name">Name</label>
        <input id="f-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-role">Role</label>
        <input id="f-role" name="role" type="text" autocomplete="organization-title" required />
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-size">Company size band</label>
        <select id="f-size" name="size" required>
          <option value="">Select a band</option>
          <option>Under 100</option>
          <option>100–499</option>
          <option>500–5,000</option>
          <option>5,000+</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-soc">Current SOC/MDR setup</label>
        <select id="f-soc" name="soc" required>
          <option value="">Select one</option>
          <option>Internal SOC</option>
          <option>MDR provider</option>
          <option>Internal SOC and an MDR</option>
          <option>Neither yet</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="f-pain">One-sentence pain</label>
        <textarea id="f-pain" name="pain" rows="3" required
          placeholder="What breaks first in your week?"></textarea>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Send application</button>
        <span class="field-note">
          Opens your mail client, addressed to {CONTACT}, with these answers filled in.
        </span>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

  <section id="faq">
    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <dl class="faq">
      <dt>Does ProSentinel replace my team?</dt>
      <dd>
        No. It removes the work your team should not be doing. The headcount you
        keep moves up the stack — incident response, threat hunting, hardening —
        and stops drowning in triage.
      </dd>
      <dt>What stack will ProSentinel work with?</dt>
      <dd>
        Target integrations for the first cohort: the major SIEMs (Splunk,
        Sentinel, Chronicle), the major EDRs (CrowdStrike, SentinelOne, Defender),
        the major identity providers (Okta, Entra, Google), and the response
        surfaces that go with them. The first cohort sets the build order — tell us
        your stack and it goes to the front.
      </dd>
      <dt>What if ProSentinel does the wrong thing?</dt>
      <dd>
        Every action is bounded by the thresholds you set, logged with full
        evidence, and reversible where it should be. We publish our autonomy
        boundaries, not just our wins.
      </dd>
      <dt>How is this different from MDR?</dt>
      <dd>
        MDR is humans plus tools. ProSentinel is a closed loop. MDR scales with
        people you can't hire. ProSentinel scales with playbooks you already have.
      </dd>
      <dt>How is this different from SOAR?</dt>
      <dd>
        SOAR runs the playbook you wrote. ProSentinel decides which playbook to
        run, runs it, and tells you what it did. The difference is judgment.
      </dd>
      <dt>Where does my data go?</dt>
      <dd>
        Into your tenant or ours, your choice. We do not train on your data.
        Architecture and data-handling docs available under NDA.
      </dd>
      <dt>What does it cost?</dt>
      <dd>
        See design-partner pricing above. Design-partner pricing now; GA pricing
        publishes with the second cohort.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section id="final-cta">
    <h2>Take back the other 22 hours.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      We're onboarding a small cohort of design partners now. One conversation, one
      scope, one measurable outcome inside 60 days.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="#design-partners">Become a design partner</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>Email the team</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="footer">
    <div class="site-footer wide">
      <p class="footer-brand">Tactical Solutions · ProSentinel</p>
      <nav class="footer-links" aria-label="Footer">
        <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
        <a href="#proof">Proof</a>
        <a href="#for-mssps">For MSSPs</a>
        <a href="#design-partners">Design partners</a>
        <a href="#trust">Security</a>
        <a href="#faq">Privacy</a>
      </nav>
      <p class="small-print">
        ProSentinel is built by <a href={withBase('/')}>Tactical Solutions</a>. The
        autonomy layer for real-world operations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // v0 submission path: compose a mailto with the field values prefilled.
  // No third-party form account and no spend. Swap to a form endpoint later
  // without changing the fields.
  const form = document.getElementById('intake') as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const CONTACT = 'business@tacticalsolutions.com';

  form?.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    const data = new FormData(form);
    const value = (key: string) => String(data.get(key) ?? '').trim();
    const lines = [
      `Name: ${value('name')}`,
      `Role: ${value('role')}`,
      `Company size band: ${value('size')}`,
      `Current SOC/MDR setup: ${value('soc')}`,
      '',
      `Pain: ${value('pain')}`,
    ];
    const subject = `Design partner application — ${value('name') || 'ProSentinel'}`;
    window.location.href =
      `mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=${encodeURIComponent(subject)}&body=${encodeURIComponent(lines.join('\n'))}`;
  });
</script>

<style>
  .hero-proof {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .aside-link { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .sub-line { color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 60ch; }
  .footnote { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .card-cta { margin-top: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .metric-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(14rem, 1fr));
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .metric {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
  }
  .metric-label {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
  .metric-value {
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .metric-desc { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .intake {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
  .intake-intro { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .field { margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .field label { font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.3rem; }
  .field input,
  .field select,
  .field textarea {
    font: inherit;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .field input:focus,
  .field select:focus,
  .field textarea:focus {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 1px;
  }
  .field-note { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
  .faq dt { font-weight: 600; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .faq dd { margin: 0.3rem 0 0; color: var(--fg-muted); max-width: 68ch; }
  .site-footer {
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem 2rem;
    max-width: 60rem;
  }
  .footer-brand { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg); }
  .footer-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .footer-links a { text-decoration: none; }
  .footer-links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .small-print { margin: 0; max-width: 60ch; }
</style>
